The image, identified as Figure 6 in the provided context, displays flow cytometry histograms demonstrating that Nano-11 enhances the expression of costimulatory molecules on dendritic cells (DCs). Specifically, DCs incubated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) for two days show a marked increase in the expression of CD80 and CD86, and a slight increase in CD40, compared to untreated control DCs (gray line). This indicates Nano-11's ability to activate DCs, which is crucial for initiating an effective immune response, thus supporting its role as a vaccine adjuvant.